 "response_text": "**30.1 percent.**\n\nFrom the table row: estimate 1,502 households, MOE ±743, SE 452.\n\n- SE = MOE / 1.645 = 743 / 1.645 = 451.7 ≈ 452\n- CV = SE / estimate × 100 = 452 / 1,502 × 100 = 30.1%\n\nThe `1` in the flag column marks it: a CV above 30% is the conventional Census threshold at which an ACS estimate is considered too imprecise to publish or interpret on its own. This cell sits just over that line — the true count could plausibly run from roughly 760 to 2,245 households at 90% confidence. If you need a usable number here, collapse it with adjacent brackets (e.g. $15,000–$24,999, which would give ~3,497 with a much tighter relative error).",
